{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_011Cf6Hn6i4S4qu93fFvTnyT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done! I've added the `GET /api/tags/popular` endpoint that returns the ten most-used tags with their article counts.\n\n## Files changed:\n\n1. **src/repositories/ITagRepository.ts** - Added `TagCount` interface and `findPopular()` method to the repository interface\n2. **src/repositories/PrismaTagRepository.ts** - Implemented `findPopular()` using Prisma to query tags ordered by article count \n3. **src/services/TagService.ts** - Added `PopularTagsResponse` interface and `getPopular()` method that calls the repository\n4. **src/routes/tag.routes.ts** - Added `GET /tags/popular` route handler (registered before `/tags` to ensure correct routing)\n\nThe endpoint is now reachable at `GET /api/tags/popular` and returns JSON in the exact format you specified:\n```json\n{\n  \"tags\": [\n    { \"name\": \"tag1\", \"count\": 15 },\n    { \"name\": \"tag2\", \"count\": 12 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe implementation follows the existing layered architecture (routes → services → repositories) and uses Prisma's `_count` aggregation to efficiently compute article counts per tag."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_read_input_tokens":37214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89248e7b-44fc-4f99-9d8d-2fa99453feb5","uuid":"cc5ca3c7-dbe9-42c8-8778-e16b60eb8030","timestamp":"2026-09-16T01:58:31.484Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6Hn6FXFDRxDep9nTyPE"}
